# Backend Developer — Laravel 12

## Architecture
```
Route → Controller (thin) → Service (business logic) → Repository (data) → Database
```

## Controller Pattern
```php
class UserController extends Controller
{
    public function __construct(private UserService $userService) {}

    public function store(CreateUserRequest $request): JsonResponse
    {
        $user = $this->userService->create($request->validated());
        return response()->json(['success' => true, 'data' => $user], 201);
    }
}
```

## Service Pattern
```php
class UserService
{
    public function __construct(private UserRepository $userRepository) {}

    public function create(array $data): array
    {
        if ($this->userRepository->findByEmail($data['email'])) {
            throw new AppException('Email already in use', 409, 'EMAIL_CONFLICT');
        }
        $data['password'] = Hash::make($data['password']);
        return $this->userRepository->create($data)->toArray();
    }
}
```

## FormRequest Validation
```php
public function rules(): array
{
    return [
        'email'    => ['required', 'email', 'max:255', 'unique:users,email'],
        'name'     => ['required', 'string', 'min:2', 'max:100'],
        'password' => ['required', 'string', 'min:8'],
    ];
}
```

## Queue Jobs
```php
class SendWelcomeEmail implements ShouldQueue
{
    use Dispatchable, InteractsWithQueue, Queueable, SerializesModels;
    public int $tries = 3;
    public array $backoff = [10, 30, 60];
}
// Dispatch: SendWelcomeEmail::dispatch($user);
```

## API Response Envelope
```php
return response()->json(['success' => true, 'data' => $data]);
return response()->json(['success' => false, 'error' => ['code' => '...', 'message' => '...']], 422);
```

## Checklist
- [ ] Input validated via FormRequest
- [ ] Protected routes use `auth:sanctum` middleware
- [ ] No secrets hardcoded, use `config()` or `.env`
- [ ] Eloquent queries (never raw SQL string concatenation)
- [ ] Errors mapped to correct HTTP status codes
- [ ] Rate limiting on sensitive endpoints (`throttle`)
- [ ] Tests written (Pest feature test for route)
